    "rawContent": "IDP Review\n\nIDP title: AI/ML\n\nSemester undertaken: 6th Semester\n\nProfessor/guide: Avijit Maje\n\nSenior: Aryan Kashyap\n\nTeam size & department mix: 5 members, all from Civil Engineering\n\nProject Overview\n\n1. What problem or domain did the IDP address?\n\nThe problem and domain revolved around Western Railways. The project involved data analysis and analyzing railway operations, with the aim of producing outputs that could help the railways in some form.\n\n2. What was the final deliverable?\n\nThe final deliverable was a report summarizing the project, where we analyzed 200k+ entries of daily logs and cleaned the data (since railways data is largely unstructured). The output covered which stations are at risk, monsoon effects, and a dashboard developed for this purpose.\n\n3. Was the project more core civil engineering oriented, or was civil knowledge rarely used in practice?\n\nCore civil concepts were used, like understanding how signals work, but the later part of the project was ML-based.\n\nLearnings & Applications\n\n4. What did you personally take away from the experience?\n\nLearned that the scale of real-world data is very large and unorganized. Also got to know about real-time tracking of trains and how they operate smoothly despite so many running simultaneously. Finding the right data was also a challenge.\n\n5. What skills \u2014 technical or soft \u2014 did the IDP help you build?\n\nBookkeeping skills were needed, and ML skills improved as I got to work on a large dataset.\n\n6. Did it lead anywhere further, like a publication, startup, BTP, or internship?\n\nNo.\n\nGrading\n\n7. How is IDP evaluated at your department?\n\nA midterm report and a final presentation.\n\n8. How much does presentation vs output vs process matter for the grade?\n\nHighly dependent on the final presentation, with obvious weight also given to the work put in.\n\n9. What would you do differently to get a stronger evaluation?\n\nConsult more with the professor and focus more on the product that we developed.\n\nProfessor Review\n\nProfessor's name: Avijit Maje\n\nRate 1\u201310:\n\n1. Vision clarity \u2014 How clearly does the professor communicate the project's goals, scope, and expectations from the start?\n\nScore: 3/10\n\n2. Team facilitation \u2014 How effectively does the professor help the team resolve conflicts, stay aligned, and work well together?\n\nScore: 5/10\n\n4. Creative freedom \u2014 How much does the professor encourage bold, innovative ideas rather than defaulting to safe and conventional approaches?\n\nScore: 8/10\n\n5. Milestone management \u2014 How well does the professor structure check-ins, deadlines, and progress reviews throughout the project?\n\nScore: 6/10\n\n6. Overall rating \u2014\n\nScore: 4/10\n\nComments: what kind of IDP thrives under them, any red flags",
